b('MCQ: R = {(1,1), (2,2), (3,3), (1,2), (2,1)} on {1,2,3} is<br>(a) reflexive only (b) symmetric only (c) transitive only (d) equivalence', 'Reflexive ✓; symmetric ✓; transitive: (1,2),(2,1) ⇒ (1,1) ✓; (2,1),(1,2) ⇒ (2,2) ✓. ' + E('(d) equivalence'))
b('MCQ: R = {(a, b) : a ≤ b} on R is<br>(a) equivalence (b) reflexive and transitive only (c) symmetric only (d) none', E('(b)') + ': partial order')
b('MCQ: on Z, R = {(a, b) : a − b is divisible by 5}. Number of equivalence classes?<br>(a) 1 (b) 2 (c) 4 (d) 5', 'One class per remainder 0–4: ' + E('(d) 5'))
b('MCQ: f : R → R, f(x) = x|x| is<br>(a) one-one, not onto (b) onto, not one-one (c) bijective (d) neither', 'Increasing (−x² for x < 0, x² for x ≥ 0), and every real is attained: ' + E('(c) bijective'))
b('MCQ: f : R → R, f(x) = sin x is<br>(a) one-one (b) onto (c) both (d) neither', 'sin(0) = sin(π), range [−1, 1] ≠ R: ' + E('(d) neither'))
b('MCQ: f : R → R, f(x) = x³ + x. Then f is<br>(a) one-one, not onto (b) many-one (c) bijective (d) neither', 'Strictly increasing (f′ = 3x² + 1 > 0) and cubic (goes to ±∞): ' + E('(c) bijective'))
b('MCQ: f : [0, ∞) → [0, ∞), f(x) = x². f is<br>(a) one-one not onto (b) onto not one-one (c) bijective (d) neither', E('(c)') + '. Compare f : R → R, where it is neither')
b('MCQ: f(x) = 2x + 3, g(x) = x². (fog)(2) =<br>(a) 11 (b) 49 (c) 7 (d) 25', 'g(2) = 4, f(4) = 11: ' + E('(a) 11'))
b('MCQ: f(x) = (x − 1)/(x + 1). f(f(x)) =<br>(a) x (b) −1/x (c) 1/x (d) −x', 'f(f(x)) = ((x − 1)/(x + 1) − 1) / ((x − 1)/(x + 1) + 1) = −2/(2x) = ' + E('(b) −1/x'))
b('MCQ: f : R → R, f(x) = 5x − 3. f⁻¹(x) =<br>(a) (x + 3)/5 (b) (x − 3)/5 (c) 5x + 3 (d) 1/(5x − 3)', 'y = 5x − 3 → x = (y + 3)/5: ' + E('(a)'))
b('MCQ: number of one-one functions from {1, 2, 3} to {a, b, c, d, e} is<br>(a) 15 (b) 60 (c) 125 (d) 243', '5 × 4 × 3 = ' + E('(b) 60'))
b('MCQ: number of onto functions from {1, 2, 3, 4} to {a, b, c} is<br>(a) 36 (b) 81 (c) 24 (d) 12', '3⁴ − 3·2⁴ + 3 = 81 − 48 + 3 = ' + E('(a) 36'))
b('MCQ: number of reflexive relations on a set with 3 elements is<br>(a) 8 (b) 64 (c) 512 (d) 9', '2^(9 − 3) = ' + E('(b) 64'))
b('Integer answer (JEE Main): number of equivalence relations on {a, b, c, d} containing (a, b)?', 'Partitions of {ab, c, d} = ' + N('5'))
b('Integer answer: n(A) = 3, n(B) = 4. Number of one-one functions A → B?', '4 · 3 · 2 = ' + N('24'))
b('Assertion–Reason.<br><b>A:</b> f : R → R, f(x) = x² is not invertible.<br><b>R:</b> f is not one-one.<br>(a) Both true, R explains A (b) Both true, R does not (c) A true, R false (d) A false, R true', E('(a)') + ': invertible ⇔ bijective; f(−1) = f(1) shows f is not one-one (and also not onto)')
b('Assertion–Reason.<br><b>A:</b> A relation on {1, 2, 3} that is symmetric and transitive is reflexive.<br><b>R:</b> (a, b) and (b, a) give (a, a).<br>(a) Both true, R explains A (b) A false, R true (c) A true, R false (d) Both false', E('(b)') + ': R is true only for elements that appear in some pair; an isolated element (like 3 in {(1,2),(2,1),(1,1),(2,2)}) breaks A')
